# Agent & MCP Server Python Conventions

## OGX agent (`doc-gen-agent/agent.py`)

- Agent logic uses the **OGX Responses API** (`AsyncOgxClient`), not
  LangChain/LangGraph — the server-side agentic loop (tool calls,
  inference) runs in the OGX sidecar container, not in this process.
- `run_agent()` is an async generator that `yield`s text chunks; always
  preserve streaming behavior (don't buffer the full response before
  returning) so the Gradio UI can render incrementally.
- All config comes from environment variables with sensible defaults
  (`OGX_BASE_URL`, `GITHUB_MCP_URL`, `MODEL_NAME`, `KNOWLEDGE_FILE`) —
  never hardcode a cluster-internal URL inline; add a new env var instead.
- Keep the token-budget guardrails in the system prompt in sync with
  `MAX_INFER_ITERS` — if you change one, reconsider the other.
- Wrap OGX stream consumption in the existing `asyncio.timeout` /
  `asyncio.TimeoutError` / broad `except Exception` pattern so a stuck
  tool-call loop degrades to a user-visible error instead of hanging.

## GitHub MCP server (`github-mcp-server/server.py`)

- Built with `FastMCP`; tools are plain `async def` functions decorated
  with `@mcp.tool()`. Docstrings are the only documentation an agent sees
  — write them as instructions to the model (when to call it, what it
  returns), not just a human-facing description.
- Every tool must return a `dict[str, Any]` with an `"error"` key on
  failure rather than raising — the agent has no way to catch exceptions.
- Respect the existing guardrails when adding new tools: cap result size
  (see `MAX_TREE_ENTRIES`, `MAX_FILE_BYTES`), and filter out
  binary/vendor paths (`EXCLUDED_PATH_PREFIXES`, `EXCLUDED_EXTENSIONS`)
  rather than returning everything and relying on the model to ignore it.
- `GITHUB_TOKEN` is optional — any new tool that requires it (like
  `search_code`) must check for it and return a clear `"error"` message
  rather than failing with a raw 401 from the GitHub API.

## General

- No test suite exists yet; after edits, at minimum run
  `python3 -m py_compile <file>`.
- Inference always goes through the OGX sidecar's `remote::vllm`-protocol
  provider (OpenAI-compatible), pointed at the endpoint configured in
  `doc-gen-agent/k8s/cluster-config.yaml` — never call an LLM API (OpenAI,
  Anthropic, etc.) directly from `agent.py`/`app.py`; add/adjust OGX
  provider config instead.
